From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:55:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 021/342] dwc2: a separate host channel for interrupt endpoints

All transfers ran one at a time on channel 0, so polling HID devices
waited behind bulk data: with a USB flash drive writing, keyboard and
mouse polls came up to 188 ms late. Transfers now go to one of two
lanes, each a host channel with its own queue, worker thread and part
of the bounce buffer: control/bulk on channel 0, interrupt endpoints on
channel 1. The interrupt handler wakes the lane whose channel halted.

Measured on the ODROID-C2 with 256 MiB written to and read from a flash
drive while a keyboard and mouse are attached: worst poll delay 7 ms
(was 188 ms), about 197 polls/s (was 150-184), throughput unchanged
(21.6 MB/s write, 41.7 MB/s read; the drive varies). A statistic in the
interrupt lane reports polls that come 20 ms or more late under load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
